forklift patch 0002 (7a-3, docs/plans/2026-11-26-7a3-sdk-arrival-stamp.md 2): the SDK's sample times from the receive
thread's byte arrival. Applied after 0001 (deploy/ros2/Dockerfile.scan), against Slamtec/sllidar_ros2 34300099.

- The receive thread stamps each read as read() returns (getus, CLOCK_MONOTONIC) and numbers it; the decoder hands
  the codec the bytes with that arrival (IAsyncProtocolCodec::onDecodeDataAt), the codec holds it while it decodes
  them, and the driver gives the unpacker the arrival of the read that completed each sample message
  (forklift::deliverDecoded). The unpacker's clock read returns it -- not the decode time, which waited in the
  receive queue. A clock read without one marks the start (arrivalMissing); grabScanDataHqWithArrival reports it.
- Every mode stamps a capsule's samples with its own capsule's arrival: Dense and UltraDense took the next capsule's
  time; their capsule and time now change together (the angle-jump discard included) and a reset drops both.
- UltraDense's sample delay used (31 - sampleIdx) for 64 samples a capsule and wrapped to ~2^32 us for the second
  half (an upstream bug); it is (63 - sampleIdx), as UltraBoost's formula is written. The other delays are unchanged.
- The node publishes scan_sdk only in the v2 format: frame_id '<frame>@sdk_mono_v2#<run>.<start>' (run: the
  launcher's forklift_run_id, 8-32 lowercase hex; start: a new random id at every scan start), only for a scan whose
  sample times all came from arrivals; each start's mode goes on 'scan_sdk_info' (std_msgs/String JSON: format,
  run, start, ans_type, sample_period_us, baudrate; reliable, transient_local). No run id, no scan_sdk.
- FORKLIFT_SDK_RX_LOG=<file> (bench only): each read (R rx_seq rx_us bytes decode_us) and each sample message
  (C rx_seq capsule_seq ans_type), queued and written by a thread of its own; lines that find the queue full are
  counted (D <n>).
- test/forklift_arrival_test.cpp (ctest, BUILD_TESTING): the real transceiver, codec, delivery and handlers on a
  fake channel, reads 80 ms apart, the decoder held 500 ms.

